# Scheduled tasks for ApostropheCMS hosting
#
# ApostropheCMS hosting reads this file on every deploy and runs the
# entries in it on a schedule. It has no effect if you host the project
# yourself. See https://apostrophecms.com/docs/guide/hosting.html#scheduled-tasks
#
# - Times are UTC.
# - Commands run from the root of this repository.
# - Schedules use five numeric fields (digits, *, ",", - and /) or one of
#   @hourly, @midnight, @daily, @weekly, @monthly, @annually. Day and month
#   names, @yearly, @reboot and VAR=value lines are not supported.
# - Your project's environment variables are available to every task.
# - To stop a task, comment out or delete its line. Don't delete this file:
#   that leaves the previously installed tasks running.
# - Each comment line shows up in the deploy log as "Ignoring unsupported
#   crontab line". That is expected.
#
# Examples. Remove the leading "# " to enable one.
#
# Every 15 minutes:
# */15 * * * * node app.js my-module:my-task
#
# Every day at 03:00 UTC:
# 0 3 * * * node app.js my-module:my-nightly-task
